<title>AUSTRALIA: MIM says two injured at Mt Isa mine.</title>
<headline>MIM says two injured at Mt Isa mine.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>MIM Holdings Ltd said two miners were injured in a blasting accident at its Mount Isa copper mine in Queensland but that production has not been affected.</p>
<p>The accident occurred at about 10.00 a.m. (0000 GMT) on Tuesday, a MIM spokeswoman told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;The mine has not been shut down and production has not been affected,&quot; the spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The two miners were admitted to a local hospital, she said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
